7. So far as criminal appeals are concerned, Rule 2 of Chapter II of the Patna High Court Rules provides that:
(a) an appeal or reference in a case in which a sentence of death has been passed;
(b) an appeal, revision or reference in which a substantive sentence of more than ten years imprisonment has been passed;
(c) an appeal under Section 378 from an order of acquittal relating to an offence punishable with death or with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment of either description for more than ten years and passed by a Court competent to pass such sentence;
Patna High Court CR. APP (SJ) No.3034 of 2017 dt. 22-11-2024 (d) an appeal under Section 377 or a case in which notice has been issued under Section 401 to an accused to show cause while the sentence should not be enhanced, shall be listed before the Division Bench of the High Court.
Md. Danish vs The State Of Bihar on 22 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/193631120/
